    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116166" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠλκα</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦλκας</span></b> , only in acc. sg. and pl., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλοξ, αὖλαξ</span>
			, <i>furrow,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.707
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.375
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				2.81
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.1054
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1333
			</span></i>. (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ ὦλκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
				</span></i>
			 l. c. has perh. replaced <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽
				Ἄϝολκα</span> which may have been an old 
				Aeol.
			 form (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀϝḷκα</span>).)</div>
